# MaCSad gateway read-route policy

This import-free leaf classifies the two exact read-only operational routes.
It does not expose either route through the HTTP adapter; it only defines the
policy that a later dependency-aware handler must use.

## To classifiedHealthRead (method: Text, path: Text) -> Bool:
    If method is equal to "GET":
        Return path is equal to "/api/v1/health".
    Return false.

## To classifiedReadinessRead (method: Text, path: Text) -> Bool:
    If method is equal to "GET":
        Return path is equal to "/api/v1/ready".
    Return false.

## To classifiedMutationRouteAvailable (routeKnown: Bool) -> Bool:
    Return false.

## Test: Health route is classified
    Let safeRoute be classifiedHealthRead("GET", "/api/v1/health").
    Let unsafeRoute be classifiedHealthRead("POST", "/api/v1/health").
    Expect that safeRoute is equal to true.
    Expect that unsafeRoute is equal to false.

## Test: Readiness route is exact GET only
    Let safeRoute be classifiedReadinessRead("GET", "/api/v1/ready").
    Let wrongMethod be classifiedReadinessRead("POST", "/api/v1/ready").
    Let lowerMethod be classifiedReadinessRead("get", "/api/v1/ready").
    Let trailingPath be classifiedReadinessRead("GET", "/api/v1/ready/").
    Let healthPath be classifiedReadinessRead("GET", "/api/v1/health").
    Expect that safeRoute is equal to true.
    Expect that wrongMethod is equal to false.
    Expect that lowerMethod is equal to false.
    Expect that trailingPath is equal to false.
    Expect that healthPath is equal to false.

## Test: Mutation routes are unavailable
    For all booleans routeKnown:
        Let available be classifiedMutationRouteAvailable(routeKnown).
        Expect that available is equal to false.
